course: dictionary
lesson: 9360
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Spoilt is a good example. In Perth, Lachlan's mate says, «You're spoilt rotten, you've got every console.» Here spoilt means a person has been given too much and behaves badly, not that they have been broken.
explain: Spoilt can also mean damaged, ruined or gone bad. A spoilt day is a day that went wrong. Spoilt milk has gone sour and is not safe to drink. The words around it, like rotten, ruined or sour, give you the clue.
explain: Spoilt is also a form of the verb spoil, so it can be used in sentences like «The rain spoilt our picnic.» Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Spoilt has more than one meaning, so check the context before you choose one.
fact: «Spoilt» can describe a child who has been given everything they want and behaves badly as a result.
fact: «Spoilt» can also mean food that has gone bad and is not safe to eat, or something damaged or ruined.
fact: In the UK, a spoilt vote is a ballot paper filled in wrongly, so it is not counted.
fact: «Spoilt for choice» means there are so many good options that it is hard to pick one. In US English, spoilt is usually spelt spoiled.
exercise: «You're spoilt rotten, you've got every console.» What does spoilt mean here? | Counted as a wrong vote | *A child who has been given everything and behaves badly | Ruined by the rain | Gone bad and not safe to eat
exercise: The milk smelled sour, so Mum said it was spoilt. What does spoilt mean? | A child who gets too many treats | *Gone bad and not safe to drink | Filled in wrongly on a form | Very happy
exercise: «There are so many good films that I am spoilt for choice.» What does spoilt for choice mean? | A film that has been ruined | Having no choices at all | Tired of watching films | *Too many good options to pick from easily
test: «Her drawing was spoilt when the paint spilled on it.» What does spoilt mean? | *Ruined or damaged | Very happy | Given everything she wanted | Counted as a vote
test: Which meaning fits a ballot paper that has been filled in wrongly and will not be counted? | Spoilt for choice | *A spoilt vote | A spoilt child | Spoilt food
exam: «The spoilt milk smelled awful.» What does spoilt mean? | Given too much and behaving badly | Ruined by a rainy day | Counted as a wrong vote | *Gone bad and not safe to drink
